---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES | Sign-Flip Street Culture, Grime Art &amp; XRP KIDs"
  description="NO BALL GAMES turns restricted-space signage into a street-culture brand built on Charlie Buster's Grime Art, original painted art, wearables and the XRP KIDs lore universe."
  current="home"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-card hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Sign flip • Grime Art • XRP KIDs</span>
      <h1>NO BALL <span class="hero-title-accent">GAMES</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The sign told us where not to play. We built a culture from that wall anyway. NO BALL GAMES is a street-culture brand rooted in UK estate energy, Charlie Buster's Grime Art visual language, original painted work, collectible clothing and the XRP KIDs universe.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}collections/`}>Explore the collection</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}about/`}>Discover Grime Art</a>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-grid" role="group" aria-label="Core pillars">
        <div class="stat"><strong>NO BALL GAMES</strong><span>sign-flip street brand</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>Grime Art</strong><span>Charlie Buster's visual language</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>XRP KIDs</strong><span>100 / 89 / 11 lore universe</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="hero-card hero-sign" aria-label="NO BALL GAMES sign graphic">
      <div class="restricted-board">
        <strong>NO BALL</strong>
        <strong>GAMES</strong>
        <span>Play anyway</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        From estate walls and blocked courts to painted jackets, original canvases and the XRP KIDs lore universe. One sign. A whole culture built behind it.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>NO BALL GAMES: the brand</h2>
      <p>A street-culture system built from restriction, rebellion and raw creative energy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">01 • The sign flip</span>
        <h3>Restricted-space rebellion</h3>
        <p>
          British warning signs, locked courts, fenced estates and blocked spaces are the raw material. NO BALL GAMES flips restriction into cultural ownership: we played here anyway, we painted here anyway, we built something here anyway.
        </p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}about/`}>Read the brand story →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">02 • Charlie Buster / Grime Art</span>
        <h3>The raw visual backbone</h3>
        <p>
          Charlie Buster's Grime Art visual language powers the painted jackets, raw portrait energy, street textures and sign-flip identity of NO BALL GAMES. Graffiti, grime music culture, estate attitude and one-of-one painted work — this is what Grime Art looks like.
        </p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}about/`}>Discover Grime Art →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">03 • XRP KIDs</span>
        <h3>The XRP lore universe</h3>
        <p>
          XRP KIDs is the XRP-side NO BALL GAMES lore branch built around 100 genesis KIDs, Alpha Aaron's capture arc, FRET's resistance, the $PMSL hard-fork shield and Block Buster OG. The sign becomes a door. The culture fights back.
        </p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Explore the XRP KIDs universe →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">XRP KIDs universe</span>
      <h2>100 genesis KIDs. 89 captured. 11 free.</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>100 genesis XRP KIDs — the foundation of the lore universe.</li>
        <li>89 captured by Alpha Aaron, the machine-control antagonist.</li>
        <li>11 free KIDs anchoring the FRET resistance and $PMSL hard-fork shield.</li>
        <li>FRET — Fresh Rapid Elite Team — the Barbican-rooted resistance network.</li>
        <li>Block Buster OG — the hidden 1/1 memory archive and Charlie Buster mind upload.</li>
        <li>New Dawn 2035 — the sign becomes a door. The free KIDs survive.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}lore/`}>Enter the lore universe →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Collect the story</span>
      <h2>Art. Wearables. Digital collectibles.</h2>
      <p>
        NO BALL GAMES spans original painted canvases, hand-painted jackets and wearable art, and the XRP KIDs digital collectible universe. Physical pieces carry the same raw Grime Art energy as the lore — gritty, British, one-of-one.
      </p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}collections/`}>View all collections →</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Join the movement</span>
      <h2>Art. Wearables. Lore. Community.</h2>
      <p>Commission original work, collect painted clothing, explore the XRP KIDs universe or join the NO BALL GAMES community.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Commission original work</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}community/`}>Join the movement</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
